#!/bin/bash
# GNOME Shell 50 has no nested mode. In --devkit mode it runs on a virtual monitor and
# mutter starts its viewer (mutter-devkit), a Wayland client on the app's compositor that
# shows the desktop from a PipeWire screencast stream.
set -u
export XDG_SESSION_TYPE=wayland XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=GNOME XDG_SESSION_DESKTOP=gnome DESKTOP_SESSION=gnome
if [ -f /usr/share/gnome-shell/modes/ubuntu.json ]; then
  export XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=ubuntu:GNOME XDG_SESSION_DESKTOP=ubuntu DESKTOP_SESSION=ubuntu GNOME_SHELL_SESSION_MODE=ubuntu
fi
export GDK_BACKEND=wayland,x11 QT_QPA_PLATFORM="wayland;xcb"
unset KDE_FULL_SESSION KDE_SESSION_VERSION KWIN_COMPOSE QT_QUICK_BACKEND
host_display=${WAYLAND_DISPLAY:-wayland-0}

# The shell uses logind only when this directory exists; the runtime has no logind.
rm -rf /run/systemd/seats 2>/dev/null

if [ ! -S /run/dbus/system_bus_socket ]; then
  mkdir -p /run/dbus && rm -f /run/dbus/pid
  dbus-daemon --system --fork || echo "== gnome: no system bus; the shell will not start"
fi

[ -f /usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas/gschemas.compiled ] || glib-compile-schemas /usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas 2>/dev/null

echo "== nos-gnome-session: GNOME on $host_display; the viewer sizes the monitor"
exec dbus-run-session -- bash -c '
  pipewire >"${BL_DEBUG_DIR:-/tmp}/gnome-pipewire.log" 2>&1 &
  for _ in $(seq 50); do [ -S "$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pipewire-0" ] && break; sleep 0.1; done
  wireplumber >"${BL_DEBUG_DIR:-/tmp}/gnome-wireplumber.log" 2>&1 &
  WAYLAND_DISPLAY='"$host_display"' gnome-shell --devkit
'
